<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh tea prices fall as major buyers absent.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh tea prices fall as major buyers absent.</headline>
<dateline>CHITTAGONG, Bangladesh 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladeshi tea prices fell on the absence of major buyers like Pakistan and Afghanistan at the weekly auction on Tuesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>Brokers said the lack of demand from overseas pushed the prices of fannings and small brokers sharply down. Buyers for Poland operated selectively.</p>
<p>The average price was 58.35 taka per kg, 1.09 taka down from the previous sale. Some 502,455 kg of teas were sold at the auction.</p>
<p>The next sale will be held on June 17 with an offer of 950,000 kg.</p>
<p>($1 = 43.65 taka)</p>
</text>
